PATCH 564: the projectile INTERACTION handlers -- all ten targets of c14f's per-type dispatch
(DGROUP:0xe518) were unpromoted, so every 2-D range contact was a hit.

bb1b (patch 284) is the "what did this projectile strike" walk: for each candidate with [+0x16]&0x40
inside 0ea9's 2-D range circle it dispatches c14f = `mov bx,[si] ; shl bx,1 ; jmp [bx-0x1ae8]`, the
per-type INTERACTION test, and takes the first candidate whose handler returns CF=1.  The port had NONE
of the ten handlers that table points at -- an indirect call into them hit the icall trap, which
returns 0 without touching g_fist_cf, so bb1b read the carry 0ea9 had just left: 1.  Every object in
the range circle "interacted", the first one in table order won, and a shell that passed within a few
hundred units of a tree, a wreck or one of AZER1's 25 type-0x10 markers detonated there instead of
flying on to the tank it was aimed at.

The handlers, decoded from the asm (DI = bb1b's self = the projectile, SI = the candidate, CF out):

  7c09 87cb 9018 97c1   types 00..03, the vehicles:  eax = [di+0xc]-[si+0xc] ; cmp eax,BAND ; jae clc ;
                        stc  -- UNSIGNED, bands 0x800 0x900 0x800 0x700 (a projectile below the target
                        never hits)
  b382 / bc32           type 0x1b structure (band 0xc00) / type 0x17 wreck (0x500), same shape
  bd69                  type 0x1a structure: band = word[0x9ebf + byte[si+0x19]*2] (per-variant height),
                        >>2 when the projectile has [+0x19]&4
  a0a1                  types 05/06: `call 0x291` random AL ; `cmp al,[0x95e4 + word[di]]` -- a hit
                        chance keyed on the PROJECTILE's type (0x80 for type 7, 0x26/0x4c for 8..13,
                        0xfd for 15) -- then a SIGNED Z band of +-0x200
  9c97                  type 0x15, the trees: `clc ; ret` -- projectiles pass through
  c31c                  the default for 18 types (04, 07..14, 16, 18, 19): `clc ; ret`

c14f now passes (si, di) as near offsets -- bb1b's DI was never threaded to it -- and the handlers set
g_fist_cf.  No other caller of c14f or of the ten exists (the asm has exactly one `jmp [bx-0x1ae8]`).

Measured against the original (board:0017): with the player idle on AZER1 the original's debrief shows
ENEMY GROUND KILLS 10 + AIR 01, GROUND UNITS LOST 04, OBJECTIVES REMAINING 08 of 13, at 5:49 -- DEFEAT.
The port before this patch: 2 enemy kills, 2 own losses, 0 objectives, over the full 15:00 -- TIME
EXPIRED, with both sides firing the whole time.  This is the mechanism by which shots stopped becoming
kills.

